(3.1  Purpose) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Informed consent is a continuing conversation, not a signature) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(event. The coordinator confirms that a prospective participant) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(understands what the study asks of them, what is known about) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(the risks, and that taking part is voluntary.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(3.2  Required elements) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(a\) A statement that the study involves research) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(b\) The expected duration of participation) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(c\) A description of procedures, marking which are experimental) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(d\) Reasonably foreseeable risks and discomforts) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(e\) Benefits that may reasonably be expected) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(f\) Alternative procedures or courses of treatment) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(g\) How confidentiality of records will be maintained) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(h\) Whom to contact with questions about the research) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(i\) That refusal to take part involves no penalty) Tj
